WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.440
On a hot summer afternoon, cities and towns are usually hotter than the nearby countryside areas.
在炎热的夏日午后，城市和城镇通常比附近的乡村地区更热。

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.760
This is not just a feeling.
这不只是一种感觉。

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.760
Some cities can be as much as 7°C hotter.
有些城市的气温可能高出多达7°C。

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.090
Scientists call this the “urban heat island” effect.
科学家把这种现象称为“城市热岛效应”。

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:26.170
This effect is closely connected with the materials used in city buildings, which usually take in large amounts of heat from sunlight during the day.
这种效应与城市建筑所用的材料密切相关，这些材料白天通常会从阳光中吸收大量热量。

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.440
Instead of cooling quickly after sunset, these materials slowly give out the stored heat into the air.
日落后，这些材料不会迅速冷却，而是把储存起来的热量慢慢释放到空气中。

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.490
As a result, cities remain warm for a lot longer.
因此，城市保持温暖的时间要长得多。

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.900
In certain situations, high temperatures can even be deadly.
在某些情况下，高温甚至可能致命。

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:48.300
To cut urban heat, many cities have turned to trees, which work like natural air conditioners in two main ways.
为了降低城市高温，许多城市已转而借助树木，树木就像天然的空调，主要通过两种方式发挥作用。

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.710
First, they provide shade, preventing streets and buildings from heating up too much.
首先，树木提供树荫，防止街道和建筑物过度升温。

00:00:54.510 --> 00:01:02.450
Second, trees cool the air through a process called transpiration—water inside the leaves enters the air, lowering temperatures nearby.
其次，树木通过一种叫作蒸腾作用的过程给空气降温：叶片内的水分进入空气，使附近的气温降低。

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:12.870
To understand how effective trees really are, researchers studied air temperature and tree cover data from nearly 9,000 cities, and the findings were surprising.
为了弄清树木的效果究竟有多好，研究人员研究了近9000个城市的气温和树木覆盖率数据，结果令人惊讶。

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.550
Trees reduce the “urban heat island” effect by almost 50% all over the world.
在全世界范围内，树木使“城市热岛效应”减弱了将近50%。

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:35.180
Since cities are usually 1–3°C hotter than nearby countryside areas, trees can lower temperatures by about 0.5–1.5°C in many places, which can have an influence on city heat during the long hot summer.
由于城市通常比附近的乡村地区热1至3°C，树木可以在许多地方使气温降低约0.5至1.5°C，这在漫长炎热的夏季能对城市的高温产生影响。

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:41.020
However, scientists warn that planting trees alone cannot completely solve the problem.
不过，科学家提醒，仅靠种树并不能彻底解决这个问题。

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:48.130
Even with large planting projects, urban trees may cut down only a bit of heat by the middle of this century.
即使开展大规模的植树项目，到本世纪中叶，城市树木可能也只能减少一点儿热量。

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.520
Because of this, experts believe cities need more solutions.
正因为如此，专家认为城市需要更多的解决办法。

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.580
For example, reflective building materials can help.
例如，反光的建筑材料能有所帮助。

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.760
At the same time, ways of cutting greenhouse gases remain necessary.
同时，减少温室气体的办法仍然是必要的。

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.380
Trees are powerful and valuable.
树木作用强大，也很宝贵。

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:09.410
They cool cities, improve air quality and make urban life more comfortable.
它们为城市降温，改善空气质量，让城市生活更加舒适。

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:15.720
But in a warming world, they work best as part of a larger plan rather than as the only answer.
但在不断变暖的世界里，树木要作为一项更大计划的一部分，而不是唯一的答案，才能发挥最大的作用。
